WEBVTT

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:06.400
They're here right behind us.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.690
Komari-kun and my Zakus.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.030
All of them.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.370
<i>He can't be serious!</i>

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.660
<i>Kyoto Fushimi's members 
are coming? All of them?</i>

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:22.710
I told you, did I not?

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:29.710
I told you so considerately before 
your situation got any worse.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.530
Huh? You're not going ahead?

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:40.310
But both of your aces are here.
 Aren't you going to go?

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:43.640
Izumi-kun, why aren't you going?

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.590
There's only each of us.

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:48.560
It's Sohoku's chance to get ahead.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.690
Chan...? Heh.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:54.400
Your chance to leave us behind.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.050
Chirp, chirp, chirp?

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.850
Don't tell me...

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:05.270
You're still a little baby-chick 
as a second-year, Chirpizumi-kun?

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:07.210
You haven't changed, Midousuji.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.210
You're smiling.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.210
I'm not falling for your diversion.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.630
Cry all you want.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:16.310
We have our own orders.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.650
Diversion? What?

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.060
Me, attempt a diversion?

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:25.520
That's not what I'm doing.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:30.330
My only regret is that

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:35.490
I won't get to see the look of overexertion
 on Chirpizumi-kun's face.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:41.370
Eyes and mouth open, like a 
deer caught in headlights!

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.540
When my Zakus pass him,
 he won't be able to do anything.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.670
He'll grunt or gasp wordlessly.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.790
That'll be the despair

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:56.440
on Crackizumi-kun's face
 when his spirit is broken!

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.680
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.770
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:32.960
<i>LINE.12  Fallen Hopes</i>

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.300
Sohoku's team has grouped up!

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.670
Their lagging member caught up!

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:42.280
Sorry I'm late.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:45.240
Teshima-san, can you accelerate right away?

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.440
Hakone Academy is...

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:52.410
Give me five seconds to catch my breath.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.420
<i>It's all right. Calm down, Shunsuke.</i>

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.630
<i>You weren't wrong.</i>

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.710
<i>My decision was fine.</i>

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.480
<i>We'll group up with 
Teshima-san and accelerate.</i>

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:03.530
<i>Then we'll pick up Naruko on the way.</i>

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:04.470
<i>It's a fine plan.</i>

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.680
<i>Kinjou-san said so last year.</i>

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.260
<i>"Sohoku is a team that supports each other."</i>

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.230
<i>And we can't support each 
other without numbers.</i>

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.670
Let's go!

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:13.530
Yeah!

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:18.690
Your true nature is within you.

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:21.810
Face yourself.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:26.210
Face reality. Think of a way 
to break through, and try it.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.990
Copying others won't lead you to an answer.

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:31.900
<i>My true nature...</i>

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.390
<i>The answer... The answer inside me...</i>

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:37.000
<i>Did I come to this conclusion myself?</i>

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.000
Don't hesitate!

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.930
<i>Waiting for Teshima-san 
was the right decision.</i>

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:43.020
<i>My decision!</i>

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:44.230
Imaizumi-kun!

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:47.050
You're going too fast.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.720
Teshima-san can't keep up.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.130
Sorry.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:54.190
<i>I'm panicking.</i>

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:57.890
<i>Damn. I've never been good at
 matching someone else's pace.</i>

00:04:57.890 --> 00:04:59.020
<i>I'm aware of that.</i>

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:01.290
<i>I don't have time to be thinking about this.</i>

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:02.280
<i>I'm in the Inter-High.</i>

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:04.690
We need to go after Hakone Academy.

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:05.240
Yeah!

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:05.990
Yeah.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:13.660
<i>I feel like I haven't gone all-out
 since I became a second-year.</i>

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.210
Huh? Imaizumi-kun,
 you don't usually complain.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:20.670
I'm not. I'm just being candid.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:25.510
Now that we're second-years, 
we've had younger members join.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:28.750
Things are noisier, and there's more to do.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:32.260
There are times I'd rather practice 
on my own, but I can't do what I want.

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:36.680
I'm still not very good at 
interacting with underclassmen.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:39.470
It's true that you don't have 
many friends, Imaizumi-kun.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:40.360
Shut up!

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.940
I prefer quality over quantity.

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:46.060
Now that I'm a second-year, 
it's only natural.

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:48.630
I know I just have to get used to it.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:52.490
Last year, I had seniors. I was unconstrained.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.410
But this year...

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.420
It feels like I have a limiter 
installed all the whole time.

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:04.130
But your Minegayama time has 
improved compared to last year.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:07.400
I know. I'm in good shape.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.130
That's why I said it's how I feel.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:12.140
It's probably just my imagination.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.230
<i>Why am I remembering this nonsense now?</i>

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:23.610
<i>Those purple jerseys I see...</i>

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.240
<i>Those riders coming up behind us...</i>

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:31.570
<i>Did Midousuji not simply 
go after Naruko earlier?</i>

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.450
<i>Was he planning to meet up with his team?</i>

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:36.980
Why aren't you going?

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:40.330
It's Sohoku's chance to get ahead.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.670
<i>Our chance...</i>

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:44.650
<i>Did I throw that away?</i>

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.180
<i>With my decision?</i>

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:48.890
What's wrong, Imaizumi-kun?

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:50.010
Is there something behind us?

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:54.140
Sohoku's ace's muscles!

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:56.250
What?

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:03.150
K-Kyoto Fushimi's coming!

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.940
They caught up!

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:06.900
They're passing us!

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:11.570
<i>Imaizumi-san...</i>

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:16.030
<i>He has such nice muscles,
 but he's such a rough person!</i>

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:18.630
Onoda! Teshima-san! Accelerate!

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:19.910
Stick to Kyoto Fushimi's butts!

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:23.160
If we ride behind them, we'll 
be able to catch up to Hakone—

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:30.070
Recover faster, Teshima-san!

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:31.630
Aren't you a climber?

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.390
Sorry...

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:44.720
<i>No. It's not Teshima-san.</i>

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:47.900
<i>I'm the one who made the wrong decision.</i>

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:51.650
<i>What was that sound?</i>

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:55.870
Crackizumi!

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:02.450
<i>What? Imaizumi-kun suddenly dropped his pace.</i>

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:03.420
<i>Imaizumi...</i>

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.660
Imaizumi-kun, are you—

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:06.390
Onoda...

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:10.120
Imaizumi's exhausted from 
riding at the front.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:12.380
He's exhausted.

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.040
That's all.

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:21.020
<i>Imaizumi-kun's... not just exhausted?</i>

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.130
Our situation couldn't be worse.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:27.080
Kyoto Fushimi's ahead of us.
 So is Hakone Academy.

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:31.220
And now we have to fight them
 without our full team.

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:31.990
Yes, sir.

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:35.090
We have to go after them to stand a chance.

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:37.240
Can you pull, Onoda?

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:41.120
Yes, sir!

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:43.080
Sohoku's coming!

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:44.960
They've fallen behind Kyoto Fushimi!

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.500
They're finally entering the tunnel!

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:52.010
<i>Imaizumi-kun...</i>

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:55.350
<i>Sohoku is a team that supports 
each other, Imaizumi.</i>

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:56.640
<i>Especially during these moments.</i>

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:01.560
Maybe I'm just saying we're okay 
to make myself feel better.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.400
But Imaizumi, believe.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:06.060
As long as we keep pedaling, 
we'll get another chance to—

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:17.320
Of course.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:22.290
If Hakone Academy hadn't passed me,
 this never would've happened.

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:24.780
Okay, you're right.

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:27.250
You're right that I'm slow to recover, too.

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:30.290
So why are you smiling?

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.380
Huh?

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:33.840
If you had caught up,

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:37.880
we wouldn't have had a problem with 
Kyoto Fushimi or Hakone Academy!

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:39.550
But you're still talking!

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.020
Imaizumi, when times get tough—

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.140
That's enough. Sorry.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.890
It's all my fault.

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:50.560
I made the wrong decision.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.840
Sorry for yelling at you.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:59.410
<i>In that moment, Naruko made the 
right decision by going ahead.</i>

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:03.270
<i>This sound again...</i>

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:09.450
<i>You think Sohoku won't get 
another chance, Imaizumi?</i>

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:13.960
<i>This is exactly when we should 
be supporting each other.</i>

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.520
Shifting from phase six to seven.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.110
Team has grouped up.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:30.530
Just as planned, we left 
the pack during the climb

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:35.980
and caught up on the downhill four kilometers
 past the tunnel, Midousuji-kun!

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:39.860
<i>Kyoto Fushimi actually got all 
six of their members together!</i>

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:43.370
Yeah. Good work, Zakus.

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:45.610
So, what happened?

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:50.120
Did Izumi-kun say anything 
when you passed him?

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.460
<i>Hotshot!</i>

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:54.630
Nothing in particular.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:58.690
He just grunted and gasped with 
a surprised look on his face.

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:00.130
Hear that...

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:03.140
Naruko-kun?

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:09.350
Sohoku's been completely scattered!

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:12.200
Let's move onto phase eight!

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:15.480
After Hakone Academy! Accelerate!

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:16.990
Damn it!

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:18.110
<i>I knew this was coming!</i>

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:20.950
We'll pedal at the expected pace,

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:26.700
catch up within five minutes, 
and crush the champions early!

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.370
Yes, sir!

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:29.750
<i>They're accelerating!</i>

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:32.460
<i>But I'll keep up through sheer 
willpower alone if I have to!</i>

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:35.840
I need to catch up to 
Hakone Academy in the front!

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:50.980
Looks like our pursuers are coming.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:01.810
Shall I praise you, Midousuji-kun?

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:03.860
Congratulate you for catching up?

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:06.500
No need, Lashes.

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:08.540
You don't need to mind me.

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:10.950
It's been a year.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:16.170
Knowing you, I'm sure you expected 
to catch up at this exact moment.

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:19.940
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:24.630
We simply caught up after 
pedaling as hard as we could.

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:30.840
You know the second day's sprint 
line is five kilometers ahead.

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:36.870
And that exactly the 
same situation as last year,

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:39.730
when Hakone Academy tasted bitter defeat.

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:43.460
Shall we have a rematch?

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:47.700
<b>5 km to Road Race
 Second Day Sprint Line</b>

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:47.700
Hakone Academy, you can do it!

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:52.600
Let's do it, Midousuji-kun.

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:54.770
Isn't that why you came?

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:58.290
I'm sure you said you'd crush the 
champions early before chasing after us

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:01.260
at the sprint line five kilometers ahead.

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:03.450
No. No, no.

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:05.050
We didn't come to crush you.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:09.140
We're just here to practice with our betters.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.520
Our betters.

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:13.100
You're all too common during the summer...

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:16.230
You champion maggots!

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:19.970
That's not the attitude of one come 
to practice with their betters.

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:21.820
If you're coming, send your best sprinter.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:26.780
Hakone Academy will mow him down.

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:28.530
Doubashi!

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:35.360
<i>Doubashi Masakiyo! They're sending him?</i>

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:36.520
<i>He's got the green number tag!</i>

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:39.790
<i>He won yesterday's first 
result on the sprint.</i>

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.500
<i>The Road Monster, Doubashi Masakiyo.</i>

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:46.470
<i>Even as another sprinter,
 his riding seems exceptional.</i>

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:49.460
<i>He's Hakone Academy's heavyweight sprinter.</i>

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:52.720
The team is counting on you.

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:57.480
I'll be leaving you briefly, 
for about five kilometers.

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:00.610
I'm going to have some fun
 with Andy and Frank

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:04.480
as Hakone Academy's proud ace sprinter.

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:06.990
Me, Izumida Touichirou!

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:09.790
<i>I-Izumida?</i>

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:12.080
<i>The ace sprinter himself is going?</i>

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:13.430
Come on.

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:14.790
Come on! You see this?

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:17.140
My right pec, Andy!

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:19.460
My left pec, Frank!

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:23.210
They're excited now... by this battle!

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:26.870
Those were Izumida-san's pec squats.

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:29.840
He's never been beaten after doing that.

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:33.100
They call them the Squats of Death!

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:37.480
Everyone who sees it always 
laughs at how comical it looks.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:41.220
But that amusement turns 
to fear in an instant.

00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:44.570
He shoots ahead like a ray of light 
with his spring-like muscles.

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:48.820
Their smiles collapse, and they tremble,
 rooted in place.

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:50.950
Izumida-san has changed!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.990
He's gotten even stronger!

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:58.910
Will you laugh at Andy and 
Frank, too, Midousuji-kun?

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:00.600
I won't laugh.

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:06.490
Those who can only judge others 
by their comical appearance

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:09.170
are trash who can't see 
a person's true nature.

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:13.530
I guess we'll send our own special man.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:15.400
There's no need to put on airs.

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:16.630
It's you, isn't it?

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:19.980
Kyoto Fushimi's ace, #111, Midousuji-kun.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:22.600
Gross.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:26.820
You used Doubashi-kun 
to put on airs yourself.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:29.870
It was just a demonstration 
before we started.

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:31.570
Isn't it more fun that way?

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:36.180
It's time for revenge...

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:38.240
In exactly the same situation as last year.

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:40.250
It only seems similar.

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:43.170
Between last year and this year,
 everything is different.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:46.010
I'll keep my zipper zipped up to start with.

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:48.340
Against you, I'll have to go all out.

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:49.460
Don't!

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:54.430
<i>What? The guy in the back is coming.</i>

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:57.010
Don't zip up your zipper!

00:15:57.480 --> 00:16:00.150
<i>That's #116, Kishigami Komari!</i>

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:00.730
He's trying to—

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:03.060
Watch out, Touichirou!

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:03.980
Muscles!

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:05.690
He's trying to touch you!

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.760
Muscles, muscles!

00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:10.320
Muscles!

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:12.820
Kishigami!

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:14.280
What are you doing?!

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:16.170
My Frank!

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:27.210
Sorry. The heat made me dizzy.

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:29.920
First-year, that's the same 
excuse you used before!

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:35.120
With the way you keep 
showing off your muscles,

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:38.010
how could you expect me to sit still?

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:44.200
These are... These are...

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:47.860
Good muscles! I knew it!

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:52.900
Midousuji-san, can I go 
after this muscular man?

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.070
What?

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.740
<i>He wants to race for the sprint line?</i>

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:58.780
<i>#116?</i>

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:00.740
<b>4000m to Road Race
 Second Day Sprint Line</b>

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.740
You can do it!

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:02.750
You'll win this year!

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:08.130
You really don't have any restraint.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:12.130
<i>Kishigami Komari...</i>

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:15.340
Kyoto Fushimi subbed out 
one of their members?

00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:17.300
This is the new list.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:25.270
<b>114  Funazu
 115  Kiriya
 116  Kishigami Komari</b>

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:22.840
They swapped out third-year Hironishi 
for first-year Kishigami?

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:25.270
Is Hironishi not feeling well?

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:27.420
What do you think, Takadajou?

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:29.110
It's a strategic move.

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:32.320
Honestly, Hironishi's not strong.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:35.080
Kyoto Fushimi has a shallow pool 
to draw from this year.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:39.320
We knew this, but Hironishi 
was removed specifically.

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:43.440
This move will bring their members, excluding 
Midousuji, into line with one another.

00:17:43.440 --> 00:17:45.160
Do we have any data on this first-year?

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:48.960
None. But according to rumors,
 he's been brought along to every race.

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:51.130
A sub's a sub.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:53.050
He can't be that good.

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:55.160
It's nothing to worry about, Izumida-san.

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:56.220
No, I'll hear it.

00:17:57.110 --> 00:17:59.470
<i>He could be the eye of the storm.</i>

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:06.980
Supposedly, Kishigami tags along to 
every race and gives them massages.

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:13.230
I can still feel it all the 
way in my elbow, Izumida-san!

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:16.090
<i>He seems to be more than a mere masseuse.</i>

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:18.730
<i>He's an unknown value. 
We have no data on him.</i>

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:19.800
<i>But that's—</i>

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:20.660
Touichirou!

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:22.850
This race has a long way to go.

00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:25.370
The six of us can ride 
through the sprint together.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.940
The way he touched you wasn't normal.

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:29.240
Before he does anything else to you—

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:32.070
It's fine, Yuki. We're the champions.

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:33.250
We're Hakone Academy.

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:37.130
We accept and defeat all challengers.

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.380
That's what champions do.

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:41.350
If we lack data on our opponents,

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:43.210
we can learn by battling them!

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:44.390
Abs!

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:47.140
<i>Izumida's "abs" call is amazing.</i>

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:48.890
<i>I can feel the pressure 
all the way over here.</i>

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:52.150
<i>Izumida's gotten stronger than last year!</i>

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:55.940
<i>Will Kishigami be okay?</i>

00:18:55.940 --> 00:19:00.780
Do you want to hear me shout 
"abs" more, Kishigami-kun?

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:02.700
Yes, more!

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:04.330
Abs ready!

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:08.120
<i>Hakone Academy's ace sprinter 
is about to make his move!</i>

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:13.670
You really do lack restraint!

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:15.420
Go!

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:20.890
Abs, abs, abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:24.350
Abs, abs, abs, abs, <i>abs</i>!

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:27.250
Hakone Academy's sending 
their ace sprinter, Izumida!

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:28.690
Who is Kyoto Fushimi sending?

00:19:28.690 --> 00:19:31.730
#116! Third-year Hironishi Sakudai!

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:33.440
He's keeping up with Izumida!

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:36.020
Hironishi's amazing!

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:39.750
I'm impressed you're keeping up, 
but perhaps I went too fast.

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:42.240
Are you short of breath already?

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:44.570
Huh? What?

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:45.530
My breath?

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:48.040
I'm panting already

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:51.790
from seeing the movements 
of your muscles up close.

00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:54.790
Of course I'm panting.

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:56.210
<i>That's why he's panting?</i>

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:58.170
Then how's this?

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:00.120
Abs, abs, abs!

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:02.050
Bua, bua, bua!

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:04.390
Your "bua, bua" is great, too!

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:08.720
<i>Let's go, Andy and Frank.</i>

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:12.230
<i>If he's determined to keep up, 
then I'll break away by force!</i>

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:13.940
Bua!

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:17.320
<i>He's keeping up.</i>

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:22.060
I see. It seems you have fast reactions.

00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:26.570
The moment I prepare to accelerate, 
you're already starting to chase.

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:29.680
I can tell from the 
movements of your muscles.

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:32.830
Tiny vibrations tell me how much 
you're going to accelerate.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.710
I don't miss any of them.

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:38.130
So no matter how much I accelerate, 
your reaction will never be late?

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:41.970
After all, I won't get another chance 
to see your muscles up close.

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:46.970
<i>Frank senses that this man is dangerous?</i>

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:50.350
Did Frank-san just react?

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:53.150
<i>How does he know about Frank?</i>

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:56.310
<i>No, I'm always shouting his name.</i>

00:20:56.310 --> 00:20:58.110
<i>It's not strange that he knows.</i>

00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:02.120
I see. He's careful, is he?

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:04.360
He senses all danger.

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:09.530
Since he increases the pressure on 
your heart, he's careful and bold.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:13.040
Is that Frank-san's personality?

00:21:13.650 --> 00:21:18.000
<i>This man understands that 
much just from touching me?</i>

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:20.280
Your senses are incredible.

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:22.050
Do you know how this race will end, too?

00:21:22.410 --> 00:21:26.680
More or less, based on the 
movements of your muscles.

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:29.510
Who will win this sprint?

00:21:29.900 --> 00:21:31.010
Me.

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:35.520
Huh? Are you feeling slightly short of breath?

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:15.700
That cat...

00:23:19.910 --> 00:23:22.800
Come on. Don't be that way.

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:24.850
We're both black cats. Let's be friends.

00:23:24.850 --> 00:23:25.290
Huh?

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:28.090
Abs! Abs! Abs!

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:29.880
Andy! Frank, Frank, Frank, Frank!

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:30.840
Andy, Andy, Andy! Frank, Frank!

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>NEXT LINE  He Who Carries Guilt</i>

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
